const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"杠杆先明确分子分母",en:"Define leverage through assets and equity"},body:{zh:"作者用总资产相对权益的比例观察杠杆。当资产按市值计价而债务暂时不变，资产升值会增加权益，使这个比率下降。这种被动变化与机构随后主动借款、买入或缩减资产，是两个需要分开的过程。",en:"The paper examines leverage as assets relative to equity. With marked-to-market assets and approximately unchanged debt, appreciation increases equity and lowers leverage. That passive arithmetic is separate from subsequent borrowing, purchases or balance-sheet contraction."},reference:{url:"https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/research/staff_reports/sr328.pdf",label:{zh:"2010年12月工作论文 · §1–2",en:"December 2010 staff report · §1–2"}}},{title:{zh:"价格上升为何反而引出借款",en:"Why a price rise can induce borrowing"},body:{zh:"原文示例从资产100、债务90、权益10开始。资产升到101后，权益变成11；若仍以十倍杠杆为目标，就要增加9单位债务并买入资产，使资产达到110。这是解释机制的算例，不是实际银行的目标建议。",en:"The illustration starts with assets of 100, debt of 90 and equity of 10. Assets rising to 101 leave equity of 11. Restoring tenfold leverage requires borrowing and buying 9 more units, bringing assets to 110. This is a mechanism illustration, not a recommended target."},reference:{url:"https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/research/staff_reports/sr328.pdf",label:{zh:"2010年12月工作论文 · §2 · p. 8",en:"December 2010 staff report · §2 · p. 8"}}},{title:{zh:"出售与价格下跌可能相互强化",en:"Sales and falling prices can reinforce each other"},body:{zh:"反方向上，资产损失压缩权益并抬高杠杆，恢复目标可能要求出售资产偿债。若大量出售又压低市场价格，其他持有者的资产负债表也会走弱。反馈是否发生仍取决于市场流动性和机构行为，不能只凭会计恒等式断言。",en:"Losses compress equity and raise leverage, potentially prompting sales to repay debt. If selling depresses prices, other holders' balance sheets weaken too. The feedback depends on market liquidity and institutional responses, not on the accounting identity alone."},reference:{url:"https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/research/staff_reports/sr328.pdf",label:{zh:"2010年12月工作论文 · §2 · pp. 9–10",en:"December 2010 staff report · §2 · pp. 9–10"}}},{title:{zh:"不同部门不能混成一条规律",en:"Do not pool different sectors into one rule"},body:{zh:"论文依次比较家庭、非金融企业、商业银行和证券交易商的资产与杠杆变化，发现它们的行为模式不同。证券交易商的顺周期关系不能直接外推给家庭或全部公司，汇总前应保留部门分类和计价口径。",en:"The paper contrasts households, nonfinancial firms, commercial banks and securities dealers. Their asset–leverage patterns differ. Dealer procyclicality should not be assigned to every sector; preserve sector classifications and valuation conventions before aggregation."},reference:{url:"https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/research/staff_reports/sr328.pdf",label:{zh:"2010年12月工作论文 · §2 · pp. 4–7",en:"December 2010 staff report · §2 · pp. 4–7"}}},{title:{zh:"样本是独立投行，不是所有银行",en:"Standalone investment banks are a specific sample"},body:{zh:"作者选择当时五家独立美国投行，并从10-K与10-Q取得季度资产负债表。回购融资、逆回购资产、交易资产和权益各有角色；不能用一家普通公司的负债率或交易量替代这些项目，也不能忽略样本起始时间不同。",en:"Five then-standalone US investment banks are studied using quarterly 10-K and 10-Q balance sheets. Repos, reverse repos, trading assets and equity have distinct roles. Ordinary corporate debt ratios or trading volume cannot replace these items, and sample starting dates differ."},reference:{url:"https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/research/staff_reports/sr328.pdf",label:{zh:"2010年12月工作论文 · §3.1 · pp. 10–12",en:"December 2010 staff report · §3.1 · pp. 10–12"}}},{title:{zh:"观察日期与公开日期分开保存",en:"Separate balance-sheet dates from availability"},body:{zh:"季度末的资产负债表不是在该日就一定可供外部研究者使用。编辑建议同时保存报告期、披露日期、修订版本和机构合并变化。关联的时点一致教程只说明披露对齐，不代表平台已经提供原文的投行回购数据。",en:"A quarter-end balance sheet need not have been publicly available on that date. Editorial application: retain reporting period, release date, revisions and changes in entity scope. The as-of tutorial addresses disclosure alignment, not availability of the paper's investment-bank repo data."},reference:{url:"https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/research/staff_reports/sr328.pdf",label:{zh:"2010年12月工作论文 · §1; §3.1",en:"December 2010 staff report · §1; §3.1"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"依据2010年12月工作论文阅读历史美国金融机构，正式期刊引用不变。资产负债表扩张、市场成交活跃与货币供应不是同一流动性概念，不能据此推断当前机构状态。",en:"The December 2010 report concerns historical US intermediaries, separately from the journal citation. Balance-sheet expansion, market trading activity and money supply are different liquidity concepts; the study does not establish current institutional conditions."}};export{e as default};
